  "causebase_summary": "AEIOU Foundation’s website states the organisation was established in 2005 to provide early intervention for children aged 2–6 with an autism diagnosis. The site says AEIOU is neurodiversity-affirming, uses a mix of person‑first and identity‑first language based on feedback from a 2023 parent community study, and says it supports each child’s strengths, abilities and personal goals. Contact details on the site include a phone number (1300 273 435), an email address (info@aeiou.org.au), office hours and a street address (Level 1, 15 Astor Terrace, Spring Hill QLD 4000). The homepage includes a notice “Issued by the Liquidators of AEIOU FOUNDATION (In Liquidation) (ACN 135 897 255)”. The ACNC AIS 2023 extract in the evidence pack reports revenue of AUD 27,919,703 and total expenses of AUD 27,756,092 for the period 01/07/2022 to 30/06/2023. The website also indicates the organisation is a registered charity (CH1818), is working on a Reconciliation Action Plan, and provides an online payments option for families. The site links to social media channels and contains standard website notices about cookies and privacy.",
